# Shell scripts are scp'd to the VPS by .github/workflows/deploy.yml and executed with /bin/sh.
# A stray \r makes dash fail with a misleading "Syntax error: newline unexpected", which reads
# like a code bug rather than an encoding one. core.autocrlf already keeps the index at LF for
# anyone using the default Windows setup; this makes it explicit and independent of local config.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Go source files must use LF line endings. Windows autocrlf converts them to CRLF on checkout,
# which causes gofmt to flag them as needing formatting. This entry ensures committed LF is
# preserved in the working tree (preventing CRLF conversion).
*.go text eol=lf

# Generated artifacts whose tests compare them BYTE-FOR-BYTE against a fresh generator run
# (`role-permission-bundles.db.test.ts`'s REGEN-NO-DIFF, and the catalog's parity suites). The
# generators write LF; Windows autocrlf gives the working tree CRLF; the comparison then fails on
# `{\n` vs `{\r\n` with a diff that shows IDENTICAL content — which reads as "the artifact is stale"
# and invites regenerating and committing whitespace churn across ~1174 pairs.
#
# Same class of bug as the *.sh and *.go entries above, same fix. Diagnosed 2026-08-19 when
# REGEN-NO-DIFF failed locally while passing in CI (Linux, LF) — the giveaway that it was the
# checkout and not the content.
platform-nest/src/rbac/*.json text eol=lf
